    <h2>What one extra call a week is worth</h2>
    <p>A WordPress site comes with a hosting bill, a maintenance retainer, and plugin licenses. The leads lost to slow pages, generic markup, and a quiet week after a hack cost about 10 times as much. You never see them on an invoice.</p>
    <p>In a worked example for a typical local business, a $500 average job and one extra call a week come to $26,000 a year in potential work. At $5,000 a job, it's 10 times that. For a site of five to 15 pages and a contact form, WordPress means paying for a publishing system you don't need. It also brings security and speed problems that cost you customers.</p>

